comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T12:12:22.062Z",codex-sol,"Merged current main and retained both caller pins. No failing checks at the inspected PR head. Thread PRRT_kwDOSYpLFc63oZTO is a valid conditional concern: GITHUB_TOKEN merges do not start push workflows. Current read-only APIs show allow_auto_merge=true, required checks strict=false and no applicable branch rules. Both pinned callees refuse auto-merge unless required checks enforce freshness (sync lines 770-785; closeout lines 738-753), so it is currently unarmed. Refuse credential or repository-setting changes forbidden by this task, and do not disable CI dispatch with empty ci-workflows. Record the caveat without claiming the future token behavior is solved."
  "2026-11-16T12:23:26.337Z",codex-sol,"Read-only GraphQL confirms requiresStatusChecks=true and requiresStrictStatusChecks=false; applicable branch rules list is empty. This corroborates the current auto-merge refusal guard for the unresolved review thread. Exact caller-contract test, typecheck and tracker validation pass. The repository defines no npm lint script. Retried dependency-gated commands only after npm ci completed; quick npm suite remains running."
  "2026-11-16T12:30:18.019Z",codex-sol,"Prepared verification commit 2ce0ff9 records exact caller tests and disposition of PRRT_kwDOSYpLFc63oZTO. The current freshness guard prevents arming token-based auto-merge; no credential or settings change is made. Typecheck, caller contract, tracker validation and changelog:check pass. Quick npm tests remain running."
  "2026-11-16T12:36:40.118Z",codex-sol,"Complete PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick npm test exited 1: 320 tests, 319 pass, 1 fail, 0 cancelled/skipped/todo, duration 1094793 ms. Failure is test/persistence-context.test.ts:81: concurrent atomic import reports a live sdk-workspace-transaction lock after waiting 3077 ms and unconfirmed rollback. Focused retry also fails with the same lock at 3071 ms (1 test, 0 pass, 1 fail). Follow-up pm-jira-shared-transaction-wait owns this unchanged runtime failure. Caller tests, typecheck and changelog checks pass; no broad-suite success is claimed."
